Download Ollama in your local machine
=====================================
you must download and install the Ollama application locally on your machine first before running any terminal commands.
Step 1: Install Ollama
------------------------
Download the official installer directly from ollama.com and run the setup file.   
Linux: Open your terminal and run:
Bash
curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh

Windows: 
Step 1: Download & Install
Go to ollama.com/download/windows and download OllamaSetup.exe.
Run the executable file to install Ollama.
Once installed, Ollama automatically launches in the background (you will see an Ollama icon in your system tray near the clock).

1. Start the Ollama Service: ollama serve

2. Download and Run a Model : ollama run <model_name>

3. List downloaded models: ollama list

4. Stop a running model: ollama stop <model_name>


=>check version of ollama: ollama --version
=>Download a model without starting a chat immediately: ollama pull llama3.2
=>Remove a downloaded model: ollama rm llama3.2
=>Verify the Ollama Service in Web Browser. Since Ollama runs a local background server by default, open your web browser and navigate to: http://localhost:11434
Expected Result: You will see a plain web page that says: Ollama is running
